Sonja Kisa <marraskuu1978@yahoo.com> wrote:
>Is there a way to set an option or patch for your character to be gay
>or lesbian (or bisexual)?

Actually I was working on this a while back; orientation would be either
one of "gay" or "straight", or "male" or "female"; orientation would be
preserved through an amulet of change, so you'd have the choice of whether
or not you wanted an AoC to effectively change your preference or not as
it does at present. There's no game balance issue there, because the
current behaviour, equivalent to "straight", lets one use all foocubi with
an amulet of change; setting "male" or "female" is a slight disadvantage.

However, when I've discussed this, people have tended to feel that the
foocubus is completely in control, rather than needing some inherent
attraction. Therefore I've never bothered to tidy up and release the
patch.

>Perhaps for bi characters, the odds would be 50%/50% of generating an
>incubus or succubus.

Both kinds of foocubi are already generated. An obvious solution to the
balance issue with bisexual characters would be to generate half of all
foocubi with a severe headache. They lose out on the possibility of using
an AoC to scum all foocubi generated, but that's life...
